=== p2-windows · W7 · page:telemetry/MQTTInspector (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:telemetry/MQTTInspector   kind=page   web route=/mqtt-inspector
Web source  : web/src/features/telemetry/pages/MQTTInspectorPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — headless test toolchain functional.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client data port), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's
  idealized "MQTTInspectorPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Telemetry" is mapped onto these real
  conventions (the in-repo source of truth — DBHealthPage/ApiLogsPage/TelemetryGrid precedent). The surface
  registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("MQTTInspector"); RouteTable.cs already maps
  Page("MQTTInspector","mqtt-inspector",TelemetrySignals).
- Data source: the web single live query useMQTTStatus -> GET /telemetry (web/src/api/hooks/useTelemetry.ts).
  Ported as IMqttStatusFeed: MqttStatusClientFeed binds the generated contract client (ADR-004) via
  ApiRequest("get_api_v1_telemetry") and parses the body through MqttStatusSnapshot.FromJson; the default
  EmptyMqttStatusFeed resolves the empty broker state (established parameterless-ctor convention — see
  DBHealthPage/ActiveSessionsPage). The view-model accumulates the per-tick signal-throughput history exactly as
  the web useEffect does (skip the initial zero, append the non-negative delta of the running signal total, keep
  the last 60 samples).
- Units N/A on this surface (signal counts / batches / rate are dimensionless; broker uptime is seconds). Display
  formatting still flows through the shared SI-faithful ports: counts via NumberFormatting.Format (web fmtInt /
  fmtNumber) and the last-received relative timestamps via DateTimeFormatting.Format(DateTimeVariant.Relative)
  (web formatRelative).
- All 29 i18n keys already exist verbatim as translation.mqtt.* in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (29 rows in
  each locale, values matching the web fallbacks: "MQTT Inspector", "Streaming Vehicles", "Unable to load MQTT
  status", ...); the surface resolves them through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names. No new catalog
  rows required (same situation as W7 admin/ApiLogsPage).

